hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"8911","Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem told us, he said: Khalid bin Mukhlid told me, he said: Sulayman bin Bilal told me, he said: Suhail told me, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed the man who wears women’s clothing, and the woman who wears women’s clothing.” \the man\"""""""
"8912","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: I am Al-Nadr bin Shumail, Abd al-Samad, Wahb, and Abu Dawud. They said: We are Hisham, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed the effeminate, and said: “Expel them from Your homes.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, brought out so-and-so, and Omar brought out so-and-so."
"8913","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Abdul Malik bin Abi Suleiman told us, he said: Ata’ told us, on the authority of Jabir, he said: I witnessed prayer with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Eid. He began to pray before the sermon, without the call to prayer or iqamah. When He completed the prayer, stood up, leaning on Bilal, thanked God and praised Him, admonished the people, reminded them, and urged them to obey him, then he went on. To the women, and Bilal was with him. He commanded them to fear God, and exhorted them, and reminded them, and praised God, and praised Him, then urged them to She obeyed him, then he said: “Give alms, for the most of you is the firewood of Hell.” Then one of the lowly women with blond cheeks said: Why, O? Messenger of God? He said: “You curse a lot, and you are ungrateful to your family.” So they started taking off their jewelry: their necklaces, earrings, and rings, and threw them into the Bilal’s dress, which they give in charity"
"8914","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: I heard Dhar speaking, on the authority of Wael bin Mahana, On the authority of Ibn Masoud, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said to the women: “Give charity, for you will be the majority of the people of Hell.” A woman said: Oh Messenger of God, why, or why? He said: “Indeed, you curse frequently and are ungrateful to your spouse.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8915","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: We preserved it from Mansour, he heard it from Dhar, narrating on the authority of Wael bin Mahana, On the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Give in charity, O women, even if it is some of your jewelry, for you are more deserving of Fire.” Then a woman who was not from the women’s class said: Why is that, O Messenger of God? He said: “Because you curse frequently and are ungrateful to your spouse.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8916","Al-Fadl bin Sahl told us, he said: Dawud bin Amr told us, he said: Mansour bin Abi Al-Aswad told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Hassan On the authority of Wael bin Mahana, he said: Abdullah said: “Give charity, O women.” He did the same, but he did not raise it"
"8917","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: We are Ghandar, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Abu Raja, on the authority of Imran, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “I looked into Hell and saw that most of its people were women, and I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its people were poor.”"
"8918","Bishr bin Hilal and Imran bin Musa told us, they said: Abdul-Warith told us, he said: Ayyub told us, on the authority of Abu Raja’ al-Attaridi, on the authority of Imran Ibn Husayn said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I looked into Paradise and saw most of its people being poor, and I looked into Hell. Then I saw that most of its inhabitants were women.”"
"8919","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abdul Wahhab, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Raja’ al-Atardi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I looked into Paradise and saw most of its people being poor, and I looked into Hell and saw most of its people being women.” \"" 8920"""""
"8920","Abu Dawud informed us, saying: Ja'far narrated to us—and he is ibn 'Awn—saying: Sa'id narrated to us, saying: I heard Abu Raja' narrating, saying: Ibn 'Abbas narrated to us, saying: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""I looked into the Fire and saw that the majority of its inhabitants were women, and I looked into Paradise and saw that the majority of its inhabitants were the poor."" Yahya ibn Makhlad informed us, saying: Mu'afaa narrated to us, from Sakhr ibn Juwayriyah, saying: I heard Abu Raja' al-'Utaridi, from Ibn 'Abbas."
"8921","And Muhammad bin Muammar told us, he said: Othman bin Omar told us, he said: Hammad bin Najih told us, on the authority of Abu Raja’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its people were weak,” and Yahya said: “The poor.” And I looked into Hell. Then I saw that most of its inhabitants were women.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8922","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Khalid, on the authority of Sulayman al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “I looked into Paradise, and behold, many of its people were poor, and behold, the hard-working people were imprisoned, and I looked into Hell. Then the majority of its inhabitants are women.”"
"8923","Nusayr bin Al-Faraj told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakhir, On the authority of Imran bin Husayn, he said: I heard the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The majority of the people of Hell are women.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8924","Muhammad ibn al-Walid informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja`far informed us, he said: Shu`bah informed us, on the authority of Abu al-Tayyah, he said: I heard Mutarrif ibn al-Shakhir, that Imran bin Husayn narrated, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “The fewest inhabitants of Paradise are women.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8925","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Sulayman bin Harb told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Abu Ja`far al-Khattimi told us, on the authority of Amara bin Khuzaymah bin Thabit said: We were with Amr bin Al-Aas on Hajj or Umrah, and when we were passing by Dhahran, we found a woman in He brought her howdah, placing her hand on her howdah. When he descended, the people entered, and we entered with him. He said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted us in this place, and behold, we saw many crows, among which was a deaf crow with a red beak and feet. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: “No woman will enter Paradise except the number of this crow with these crows.”"
"8926","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad informed us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Abu Maslamah, he said: I heard Abu Nadhrah narrating, on the authority of Abu Saeed, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “The world is green and sweet, and God is your successor in it, to see how you do, so fear world, and beware of women, for the first temptation of the Children of Israel was with women.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8927","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yazid bin Zurayi told us, and Yahya bin Saeed told us, they said: Sulayman al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Osama Ibn Zayd, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have not left behind among the people any temptation more harmful to men than women.”"
"8928","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail narrated to us, he said: Amr bin Abi Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, left one day in the morning and went to the women in the mosque and stood over them and said: “I have never seen such deficiencies in minds.” And religion, follow the hearts of those of understanding among you. As for the deficiency in your religion: the menstruation that afflicts you, one of you will continue it, as God wills. If you remain silent, do not pray, or fast, that is the deficiency of your religion. As for the deficiency of your intellect, your testimony is only half the testimony of a woman. \Testimony.\"" Brief (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"8929","Safwan bin Amr told us, he said: We are human, he said: my father told me, on the authority of al-Zuhri, he said: Hamza bin Abdullah bin told me Omar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, complained about the time he died, he said: “Let him pray for the people.” Abu Bakr.” Aisha said: O Messenger of God, Abu Bakr is a gentle man, and he cannot hold back his tears when he reads the Qur’an, so Omar passed Ibn al-Khattab prays for the people, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Let Abu Bakr lead the people in prayer.” Aisha checked with him, and he said: “Let him pray.” “The people have Abu Bakr, so you are the companions of Joseph.”"
"8930","Zakaria bin Yahya told us, he said: Ishaq told us, he said: I am Abdul Razzaq, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Hamza bin Abdullah Ibn Omar, on the authority of Aisha, she said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fell ill, he said: “Pass Abu Bakr leading the people in prayer,” so I said: O Messenger By God, Abu Bakr is a gentle man. When he recites the Qur’an, he cannot hold back his tears. If you commanded anyone other than Abu Bakr, she would say: I can only do that. People are pessimistic about the position of the first person to take the position of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I checked with him twice, or three times, and he said: “Go through, Abu Bakr led the people in prayer, for you were Joseph’s companions.”"
"8931","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Yazid told me, he said: I am Hammad, on the authority of Ibn Sakhbra, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The most blessed of women are the ones who have the easiest in supply.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8932","Muhammad bin Jabla told me, he said: Abdullah bin Jafar told me, he said: Ubaid Allah told me, on the authority of Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Hamza bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Bad badness is found in three things: a dwelling, a horse, and a woman.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8933","Harun bin Saeed told us, he said: Khaled bin Nizar told me, he said: Al-Qasim Ibn Mabrur told me, on the authority of Yunus, Ibn Shihab said: On the authority of Hamza bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Bad badness is found in horses and women. \And the house\"""""""
"8934","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar informed me, he said: Yunus informed me, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no infection, no treason, and bad luck is found in three things: the woman, the house, and the horse.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8935","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: I am Ibn Wahb, he said: Yunus, and Malik told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Hamza, and Salem On the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There is no infection, nor treason, but bad luck is found in three people: the woman and the horse. And the house.” One of them adds the word"
"8936","Al-Harith bin Miskin read about it, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: I am Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Hamza, and Salem, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Omar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Bad bad luck is in the house, the woman, and the horse.”"
"8937","Al-Hussein bin Issa told us, he said: Ibn Abi Fudayk, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Muhammad bin Zayd bin Qunfud On the authority of Salem bin Abdullah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If it is in anything, then in the dwelling, the woman, and the horse. And the sword (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8938","Muhammad bin Khalid told us, he said: Bishr bin Shuaib told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Salem told me, that Abdullah bin Omar He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Bad badness only occurs in three things: the horse, the woman, and the house.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8939","Qutaybah bin Saeed informed us, he said: It was Abdul Wahid, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Bad badness is found in three things: the woman, the horse, and the house.”"
"8940","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The bad omen. In three: the woman, the horse, and the house.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8941","Muhammad bin Nasr told us, he said: Ayoub bin Sulayman told us, he said: Abu Bakr told me, on the authority of Sulayman, on the authority of Ibn Abi Atiq, and Musa Ibn Uqba, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salim, and Hamza, that Abdullah Ibn Omar said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Bad omen in: the horse, the woman, and the house.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8942","Muhammad bin Nasr told us, he said: Ayoub told me, he said: Abu Bakr told me, on the authority of Suleiman, Yahya said: And Ibn Shihab told me, Salim and Hamza told him that Abdullah bin Omar told them. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Bad omen is in: the horse.” And the woman, and the house.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8943","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Waki` told us, he said: Zakaria bin Abi Zaida told us, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Shaybah, on the authority of Talq bin Habib, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Ten of the fitrah: Trimming the moustache, clipping the nails, washing the knuckles, growing the beard, using the siwak, using the siwak, plucking the armpits, shaving the pubic area, And the reduction of water.” Musab said: I forgot the tenth, unless it was rinsing the mouth."
"8944","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Talaq bin Habib, mentioning “ten of the fitrah.” : The siwak, trimming the moustache, trimming the nails, washing the knuckles, plucking the armpits, circumcision, washing the anus, shaving the pubes, “And inhalation,” and I doubted “rinsing the mouth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8945","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Talq bin Habib, he said: “Ten of the Sunnah: the siwak, Trimming the moustache, rinsing the mouth, nose, trimming the beard, clipping the nails, plucking the armpits, circumcision, shaving the pubic area, And washing the anus.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: The hadith of Suleiman al-Taymi and Ja`far bin Iyas is more worthy of authenticity than the hadith of Mus’ab bin Shaybah. 5 And Mus’ab Munkar Hadith 5"
"8946","Humayd bin Masada told us, on the authority of Bishr, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Five things are part of the fitrah: circumcision, shaving the pubic hair, plucking the fingernail, trimming the nail, and shortening \the drinker\"""""""
"8947","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Saeed al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: “Five things are from the nature of the matter: trimming the nails, Trimming the moustache, plucking the armpits, shaving the pubic hair, and circumcision.”"
"8948","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Alqama, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Trim the mustache and grow the beard.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8949","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: I heard Abdul Rahman bin Abi Alqama, he said: I heard Ibn Omar says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Groom the beard and trim the mustaches.”"
"8950","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: I heard Yusuf bin Suhayb speaking, on the authority of Habib bin Yasar, on the authority of Zaid Ibn Arqam said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Whoever does not take something from what he drinks, is not one of us.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8951","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Wahb bin Jarir told us, he said: my father told us, he said: I heard Muhammad bin Abi Yaqoub, telling On the authority of Al-Hasan bin Saad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ja’far, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gave Ja’far’s family three days to come to them. Then he came to them and said: “Do not cry over my brother after today.” Then he said: “Call for me my brother’s sons.” We were brought as if we were young, so he said: “Call for me.” “The barber,” so he ordered him to shave our heads. Brief (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8952","Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, Abdul Razzaq informed us, he said: Muammar informed us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a boy who had shaved some of his hair and left some of it, so he forbade that and said: “Shave it all, or Leave him alone.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8953","Muhammad bin Musa Al-Harashi told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Khalas, on the authority of Ali, he said: “He forbade The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded a woman to shave her head.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8954","Imran bin Yazid told me, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Abi al-Rijal told us, on the authority of Omar bin Nafi’, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abd Allah Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God Almighty has forbidden me from qaz’a.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8955","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Muhammad bin Bishr, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Umar bin Nafi’, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar. He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade qaz’a.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8956","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Omar bin Nafi’ told me, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade slander.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8957","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said, Ubayd Allah told me, on the authority of Nafi’, that he told him, He heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbidding qaz’.”"
"8958","Ahmad bin Suleiman told us, he said: Abu Dawud, who is Al-Hafari, told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade qaz’a.”"
"8959","Ahmad bin Abdah told us, he said: I am Hammad, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade About disgust.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: The hadiths of Yahya bin Sa`id and Muhammad bin Bishr are more worthy of being correct than those after them, and God knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8960","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Sufyan, the brother of Qabisah, and Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, they said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb On the authority of his father, on the authority of Wael bin Hajar, he said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I had hair, and he said: “Flies,” so I thought he meant me. So I took some of my hair, then I went to him, and he said to me: “I did not mean to you, and this is better.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8961","Qutaibah told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Rabi’ah, on the authority of Anas, that he heard him say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “was not “By the long and distinct one, nor by the short one, nor by the white and albino, nor by the human being, nor by the curly cat, nor by the black one.” Brief"
"8962","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Wahb bin Jarir told us, he said: Ubayy told us, he said: I heard Qatada speaking, on the authority of Anas, he said: It was “poetry.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had a man’s hair, neither curly nor straight, between his ears and his shoulders.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8963","Ali bin Khashram informed us, saying: I am Isa, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Hassan bin Atiya, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us and saw a man with unruly hair. He said: “Doesn’t this man have something to calm his hair with?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8964","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Omar bin Ali bin Muqaddam told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Abu Qatada, he said: He had a huge group, so he asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he ordered him to treat it well, and to get off every day. \. Abu Abdul Rahman said: This is more like the truth"
"8965","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Daoud Al-Awdi, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman Al-Himyari, he said: I found A man who accompanied the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, as Abu Hurairah accompanied him, for four years. He said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade us from “One of us combs every day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8966","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mughaffal, he said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade dismounting unless it is foolish.”"
"8967","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, “forbade dismounting except foolishly.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8968","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled bin Al-Harith told us, on the authority of a whisper, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, he said: There was a man from The Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was working in Egypt. A man from his Companions came to him and saw that he was disheveled and his head was shining. I said: Why should I see you? Mishaana, and you are a prince? ! He said: The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade us from luxury.” We said: What is luxury? He said: Walking every day. Abu Abdul Rahman said: He named him: Saeed bin Iyas Al-Jariri. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8969","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Ibn Ulayya told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, that a man from the Prophet’s companions prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He is called Ubaid. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to “forbid us from much luxury.” Ibn Buraydah was asked about luxury, and he said: It includes dismounting. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8970","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Al-Ash’ath told me, he said: I heard my father speaking, on the authority of Stolen, on the authority of Aisha, and he mentioned that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “loved men as long as he was able to purify himself and put on shoes. And he dismounted.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8971","Muhammad bin Muammar told us, he said: Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Bishr, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Ash-Sha’atha’, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Yazid, on the authority of Aisha, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “loved the right hand, took with his right hand, gave with his right hand, and loved Al-Tayman in all its affairs.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And the one before him is more deserving of what is correct. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8972","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: I am Ismail, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, he said: “The hair of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, reached half his ears.” \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"8973","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, he said: It was “poetry.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to the middle of his ears.”"
"8974","Muhammad bin Muammar told us, he said: Hibban told us, he said: Hammam told us, he said: I Qatada, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was \His hair reaches to his shoulders.\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"8975","Hajib bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Waki’, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: “I have never seen anyone with better knowledge in The robe of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he has hair that reaches down to his shoulders.”"
"8976","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ammar told us, he said: Al-Mu’afāf told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: “What I saw someone more beautiful in a red suit than the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his skullcap hit his shoulders.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8977","Abdul Hamid bin Muhammad told us, he said: Mukhlid bin Yazid told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Al-Baraa told me, he said: “What I saw a man who was better dressed than the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8978","Ali bin Al-Hussein Al-Darahimi informed us, on the authority of Umayyah bin Khalid, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “is a tall man, broad between his shoulders, with a thick beard, with ruddy hair over his head, his brim to the lobes of his ears. I saw him in a red suit, and I have never seen anything better than him.”"
"8979","Al-Hasan bin Ismail bin Suleiman Al-Mujalidi Al-Masisi told us, saying: Abdah bin Suleiman told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq. On the authority of Hubayra bin Yarim, he said: Abdullah bin Masoud said: “Who do you command me to recite upon? I have recited to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” And seventy-two surahs were recited upon him, and Zayd was the owner of two wolves, playing with the boys."
"8980","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Saeed bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Abu Shihab told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Abu Wael, he said Ibn Masoud addressed us and said: “How do you command me to recite as Zayd ibn Thabit recites, after I recited from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? And he recited seventy-odd surahs, and that Zaid had two wolves with the boys?"
"8981","Ibrahim bin Al-Mustamir told us, he said: Al-Salt bin Muhammad Abu Hammam told us, he said: Ghassan bin Al-Aghar bin Husayn Al-Nahshali told us, He said: My uncle Ziyad bin Al-Husayn told me, on the authority of his father, that he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Medina, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: May God bless him and grant him peace: “Come closer to me.” He approached him, put his hand on his hair, then extended his hand, and I said blessings upon him, and prayed for him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8982","Ahmad bin Harb told us, he said: Qasim told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wael bin Hajar, He said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I had a crowd. He said: “Flies,” so I thought he meant me, so I went off and took some of my hair. He said: “ I did not mean to you, and this is better.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8983","Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to let his hair down, and the polytheists used to part their hair, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to let his hair down. He loves agreement with the People of the Book, so long as he has not been commanded to do anything about it. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, separated after that.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8984","Al-Harith bin Miskin read about it, and I hear, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ziyad bin Saad, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that He heard him say: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, lowered his forelock as God wished, then he separated after that.”"
"8985","Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Haywa bin Shurayh, and another person before him mentioned, on the authority of Ayyash bin Abbas. Al-Qatbani, that Shayyam ibn Bitan told him that he heard Ruwayfa ibn Thabit saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Ruwaifa’ Perhaps your life will be long after me, so tell the people that he is the one who tied his beard, or tied a string, or cleansed himself with the dung of an animal, or... Bone, for Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, is innocent of it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8986","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz al-Darawardi al-Madani, on the authority of Amara bin Ghaziyah, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of His father, on the authority of his grandfather, said that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade plucking gray hair.”"
"8987","Ubayd Allah bin Saad told us, he said: My uncle told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Abu Salamah said: Indeed, Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. H And Yunus bin Abdul-Ala informed us, he said: Ibn Wahb informed us, he said: Yunus informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Salamah Ibn Abd al-Rahman told him on the authority of Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Jews and Christians do not dye their hair. So they differed from them.” Ubayd Allah said in his hadith: They do not dye. Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Huraira, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a similar"
"8988","Al-Hussein bin Harith told me, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa informed us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Jews and Christians do not dye their hair, so they disagreed over them, so dye their hair.”"
"8989","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, and Sulayman bin Yasar, that they heard Abu Hurairah It is reported that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Jews and Christians do not dye their hair, so differ from them.”"
"8990","Ali bin Khashram told us, he said: Issa, who is Ibn Yunus, told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sulayman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The Jews and Christians do not dye their hair, so differ from them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8991","Othman bin Abdullah told me, he said: Ahmad bin Janab told us, he said: Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father On the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Change gray hair, and do not imitate the Jews.”"
"8992","Humaid bin Mukhlid bin Zanjawayh bin Al-Hussein told us, he said: Muhammad bin Kanasa told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of Othman bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Zubayr, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Change gray hair, and do not resemble the Jews.” \. Both of them are not preserved"
"8993","Abd al-Rahman ibn Ubayd Allah al-Halabi informed us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, who is Ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Karim, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas attributed it to the Prophet, because he said: “There are people who dye their hair black in the end of time, like the remains of doves, who will not smell the scent of Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8994","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told me, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: It came Abu Quhafa on the day of the conquest of Mecca, and his head and beard were white as white as a gap. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Change this.” “Something, and avoid blackness.”"
"8995","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Ezra told us, and he is Ibn Thabit, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: It was brought The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw Abu Quhafa, and his head and beard were as if they were thick, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “Change This, and dye his beard.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8996","Muhammad bin Muslim bin Wara Al-Razi told us, he said: Yahya bin Ya’la told us, he said: My father told us about it, on the authority of Ghaylan bin Jami’, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Abu Dhar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “The best thing that changes the hair is henna.” And concealment (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8997","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad Al-Dili, on the authority of Abu Dhar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The best thing you can do is change the gray hairs with it.” “Henna and katam” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8998","Qutaybah told us, he said: Abtar told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad Al-Dili, on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The best thing you can use to change gray hair is henna and katam.”"
"8999","Muhammad bin Abdul-Rahman bin Ash’ath told us, he said: Muhammad bin Issa told me, he said: Hushaym told us, he said: Ibn Abi told me Layla, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, Hushaym said: I met Al-Ajlah and he told me, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad Al-Dili, on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The best things to change gray hair are: henna and katam.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9000","Qutaibah told us, he said: Abtar told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad Al-Dili, on the authority of Abu Dharr, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best thing with which you can change gray hair is henna and katam.”"
"9001","Humayd bin Masada told us, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, he said: Al-Jariri told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The best things to change gray hair are: henna and katam.”"
"9002","Humayd bin Masada told us, he said: Sufyan, who is Ibn Habib, told us, on the authority of Khams, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, he said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The best things to change gray hair are: henna and katam.”"
"9003","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: I heard a whisper speaking, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, that he had been informed that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “The best things that change gray hair are henna and katam.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9004","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Iyad bin Laqit, on the authority of Abu Ramtha He said: My father and I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he had “smeared his beard with henna.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9005","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Iyad bin Laqit, on the authority of Abu Ramthah, may God be pleased with him, He said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I saw him “smearing his beard with yellow.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9006","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Darawardi told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, he said: I saw Ibn Umar dyeing his beard in good manners. It was said to him: O Abu Abdul Rahman, you are making your beard turn yellow with good manners! He said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, dyeing his beard with it, and there was no dye more beloved to him than it. He dyes all his clothes with it, even his turban.”"
"9007","Yahya bin Hakim Al-Basri told us, he said: Abu Qutaibah told us, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Dinar told us, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam, on the authority of Ubaid, who is Ibn Jurayj, who said: I saw Ibn Umar dyeing his beard, so I told him about that, and he said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said hello, “whistles at it.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: This is more correct than the one before it, and God knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9008","Abdah bin Abd al-Rahim al-Marwazi told me, he said: I am Amr bin Muhammad al-Anqari al-Kufi, he said: I am Ibn Abi Rawad, on the authority of Nafi’, On the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to wear sandals on the Sabbath day, and dye his beard with roses and saffron.” Ibn Umar did that (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9009","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, that he asked him: Did he dye his hair? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: “He did not reach that point, but there was something in his temples.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9010","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abd al-Samad told us, he said: al-Muthanna told us, he said: Qatada told us, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: May God bless him and grant him peace, “He did not dye his hair, but the hair was a little at the neck, a little at the temples, and a little at the head.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9011","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: I heard Al-Rukain speaking, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Hassan, on the authority of his uncle Abdul Al-Rahman bin Harmala, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “disliked ten things: yellowness,” meaning Immoral behavior, changing one’s hair, pulling the garment, wearing gold, striking with heels, displaying fine hair, and adornment other than what is appropriate. And ruqyah is only by means of exorcisms, the wearing of amulets, the removal of water from the wrong place, and the corruption of a child other than his mahram.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9012","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Al-Mu’alla bin Asad Al-Basri, brother of Bahz bin Asad, told us, he said: Muti’ bin Maimun told us, he said: Safiya bint Asma told us, on the authority of Aisha, that a woman extended her hand to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a letter, and he took his hand. She said: O Messenger of God, I extended my hand to you with a letter, but you did not take it. He said: “I did not know whether it was the hand of a woman or the hand of a man?” She said: Rather, it is a woman’s hand. He said: “If you were a woman, you would change your nails with henna.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9013","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Abu Zaid Saeed bin Al-Rabi’ told us, he said: Ali bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: I heard Karima, she said I heard Aisha, and a woman asked her about dyeing with henna, and she said: There is nothing wrong with it, but I hate it because my beloved, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him “He hated its smell,” meaning: the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9014","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam informed us, saying: My father and Abu al-Aswad al-Nadr ibn Abd al-Jabbar informed us, saying: Al-Mufaddal bin Fadalah told us, on the authority of Ayyash bin Abbas Al-Qabbani, on the authority of Abu Al-Husayn Al-Haytham bin Shafi, and Abu Al-Aswad said: Shafi was healed. He heard him say: I and a friend of mine called Abu Amer, a man from Ma’afir, went out to pray with Ilya’, and he was their storyteller. A man from Al-Azd, called: Abu Rayhana, one of the Companions. Abu Al-Hussein said: My companion preceded me to the mosque, then I overtook him, so I sat down. To his side, he said: Have you heard the stories of Abu Rayhana? So I said no, and he said: I heard him saying: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade ten things: brushing, tattooing, and plucking. And about a man having intercourse with another man without feeling, and about a woman having intercourse with a woman without feeling, and for a man to make the bottom of his clothes silk. like foreigners, or he puts on his shoulders silk like the likes of foreigners, and abstains from plundering, and abstains from riding tigers, and wears rings, except for that which \Sultan\"""""""
"9015","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman bin Awf, he said: I heard Muawiyah, While he was on the pulpit in the city, he took out a piece of poetry from his sleeve and said: O people of the city, where are your scholars? I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbidding such things, and he said: “The Children of Israel were destroyed when their women took \Like this\"""""""
"9016","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Muhammad bin Bashar told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ja’far, who said: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, he said: Muawiyah came to Medina and addressed us, and he took out a hair ball and said: “I did not see anyone doing that except the Jews. It was reported to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he called it falsehood. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9017","Amr bin Yahya bin Al-Harith Al-Homsi informed us, saying: Mahboub bin Musa told us, saying: Ibn Al-Mubarak informed us, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Al-Qaqa’a, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Muawiyah, that he said: O people, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade you from False, he said: “And he brought a black rag and threw it in their hands, and said: ‘This is what the woman should put on her head, then \You are brewing against him\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"9018","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khalid told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: Qatada told us, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, on the authority of Muawiyah He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade falsehood.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9019","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahim Al-Barqi told us, he said: Asad bin Musa told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Abi Abdullah Al-Dastawai, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ibn Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Muawiyah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade falsehood, And falsehood: a woman who turns her hair around.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9020","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh informed us, saying: Ibn Wahb informed us, saying: Makhramah ibn Bukayr informed me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Saeed Al-Maqbari said: I saw Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan on the pulpit, and he had in his hand one of the women’s hair kibbis, so he said: What’s the matter? Muslim women do this? I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Any woman who adds hair to her head that is not from her, then it is falsehood that she adds.”"
"9021","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, he said: Fatima bint Al-Mundhir told me, on the authority of Asma’, A woman came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, a daughter of mine has a wedding ring, and she complained, so it was torn. Her hair, is there any blame on me if I touch her hair? He said: “May God curse the one who is connected and the one who is always here.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9022","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Abu Al-Nadr told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of His wife Fatima, on the authority of Asma’ bint Abu Bakr, said that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “cursed the woman who is connected and the woman who is the one who is connected.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9023","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “Cursed The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “the one who is connected, the one who is connected, the one who has the tattoo, and the one who has the tattoo.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9024","Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem told us, he said: Abdullah, who is the son of Muhammad bin Asma, told us, he said: Juwayriyah bin Asma told us, On the authority of Al-Walid ibn Abi Hisham, on the authority of Nafi’, that he was informed that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “cursed the hyphenated woman and the one who hastily said, And the tattooer, and the tattooed woman.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9025","Muhammad bin Wahb told us, he said: Miskin bin Bukayr told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muslim On the authority of Safiya bint Shaybah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “May God curse the one who is connected and the one who is connected.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9026","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Khalaf bin Musa told us, he is the blind son of Musa, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ezra, On the authority of Al-Hasan Al-Arni, on the authority of Yahya ibn Al-Jazzar, on the authority of Masruq, that a woman came to Abdullah ibn Masoud and said: I am a woman. Leaders, is it okay for me to straighten my hair? He said: No, she said: Is it something you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, or do you find it in the Book of God? He said: No, but I heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I find it in the Book of God."
"9027","Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam told us, he said: Abu Dawud al-Hafari told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed the tattooed women, the tattooed women, the tattooed women, and the unveiled women. “For the good things that change.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9028","Muhammad bin Bashar told me, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, He said: “May God curse the women who make faces and reveal themselves. Should I not curse the one who cursed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace?!” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9029","Ahmad bin Saeed Al-Rabbati told me, he said: Wahb bin Jarir told us, he said: My father told us, he said: I heard Al-A’mash narrating, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, cursed the women who have tattoos, the women who reveal their faces, the women who reveal their hair, and the women who change their hair.” God's creation"
"9030","Ahmad bin Yahya bin Muhammad told us, he said: Omar bin Hafs told us, he said: Abi told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah. On the authority of Abdullah, he said: “May God curse the women who are retouched, the women who make tattoos, and the women who alter the creation of God,” so a woman came to him. She said: Are you the one who says such and such? He said: Why should I not say what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said? !. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: The hadith of Mansour is more likely to be authentic, and God knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9031","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jafar told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Sulayman Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He was a servant God, he says: “God has cursed the tattooed women, the women who reveal their faces, and the women who reveal their faces. Shall I not curse the one who curses the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace?!” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9032","Ahmad ibn Harb told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah said: “May God curse the women who spread their hair.” The chain of the hadith"
"9033","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Aban, who is Ibn Sama’a, told us, on the authority of his mother, she said: I heard Aisha, It says: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the tattooing woman, the tattooed woman, the waslha woman, the one with the tattooed woman, the tattooed woman, the hyphenated woman, the one with the incomplete tattoo, and the ingrown woman. And Al-Mutanamisa (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9034","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suleiman, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Murrah talking, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Abdullah, said: “The one who consumes usury, and the one who pays it, and the one who writes it, if they know that, and the one who tattoos it, and the one who tattoos beautiful things.” “The one who collects charity, and the apostate Arab after the migration, will be cursed according to the tongue of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the Day of Resurrection.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9035","Ziyad bin Ayyub informed us, he said: Hushaym told us, he said: Husayn, Mughirah, and Ibn Aoun informed us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Harith, On the authority of Ali, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “cursed the one who consumes usury, the one who pays usury, the one who writes it down, the one who withholds charity, and he used to forbid lamentation.”"
"9036","Humayd bin Masada told us, he said: Yazid told us, meaning Ibn Zuray’, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Harith, he said: “Muhammad was cursed May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: the one who consumes usury, the one who pays usury, the one who witnesses it, the one who writes it down, the woman who tattoos it and the woman who tattoos it. He said: I said: Is there a disease? He said: Yes, “and the one who makes what is permissible and what is made permissible for him, and who prevents charity, and he forbade lamentation,” and he did not say: “cursed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9037","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Khalaf, meaning Ibn Khalifa, told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed May God bless him and grant him peace, the one who consumes usury, the one who pays it, the one who writes it down, the two witnesses to it, the one who makes it lawful, the one who makes it lawful, the one who gives usury, and He forbids wailing, And he did not curse his companion.”"
"9038","Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: Jarir informed us, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Omar was brought By a woman smelling, he said: I adjure you by God, has any of you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? Abu Hurairah said: So I said: O Commander of the Faithful, I heard him. He said: What did you hear? So I said: I heard him say: “Do not smell bad, and do not get tattooed.”"
"9039","Abu Ali Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Maruzi told us, saying: Abdullah bin Uthman told us, on the authority of Abu Hamza Muhammad bin Maymun Al-Sukkari, On the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of al-Aryan ibn al-Haytham, on the authority of Qubaisa ibn Jabir, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: I heard the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “Cursed are the women who embellish themselves, the women who reveal themselves, and the women who have tattoos who change the creation of God Almighty.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9040","Muhammad bin Muammar told us, he said: Yahya bin Hammad told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Al-Aryan bin Al-Haytham, on the authority of Qubaisa bin Jabir, said: Abdullah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “cursing women who reveal themselves to women.” \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"9041","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, he said: I am Al-Hussein bin Waqid, he said: Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Al-Aryan ibn Al-Haytham, on the authority of Qubaysah ibn Jabir, who said: Ibn Masoud said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “May God curse the women who embellish themselves, those who show off, and those who wear tattoos who change the creation of God Almighty.”"
"9042","Muhammad bin Hatim Al-Marwazi told us, saying: Hibban bin Musa Al-Marwazi told us, saying: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Haywa bin Shurayh, he said: Ayyash bin Abbas Al-Qatbani told me, on the authority of Abu Al-Husayn Al-Himyari, that he told him that he and a friend of his were staying Abu Rayhana, they learn well from him. He said: My friend came one day, but I did not attend. So my friend told me that he heard Abu Rayhana say: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade licking, tattooing, and plucking.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9043","Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh told us, he said: I am Ibn Wahb, he said: Al-Layth informed me, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of my father Al-Husayn Al-Himyari, on the authority of Abu Rayhana, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade tattooing and tattooing.”"
"9044","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Al-Husayn Al-Himyari, on the authority of Abu Rayhanah, He said: We have learned that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade tattooing and tattooing.”"
"9045","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, saying: Dawud, who is the son of Abd al-Rahman Abu Sulaiman al-Attar, told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, among the best of your ankles is ithmid. \It sharpens sight and makes hair grow.\"""""""
"9046","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abu Dawud, who is Al-Tayalisi, told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Simak, he said: I heard Jabir bin Samura, he was asked about the gray hair of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “When he oiled his head, some of it would not be seen, and if he did not oil it, some of it would be seen.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9047","Muhammad bin Ali bin Maymun Al-Raqqi told us, he said: Al-Qanabi told us, he said: Abdullah bin Zaid told us, on the authority of his father, that Ibn Umar, He was dyeing his clothes with saffron, and he was told: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was “dying.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9048","Abu Ubaidah bin Abi Al-Safar told us, on the authority of Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith, he said: Bakr al-Muzliq narrated to us, he said: Abdullah narrated to us Ibn Ataa Al-Hashimi, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ali, said: I asked Aisha: Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, use perfume? She said: Yes, “remembering perfumes: musk and amber.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9049","Ahmad bin Suleiman told us, he said: Abu Dawud, meaning Al-Hafari, told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of a man, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Men’s perfume is what its scent is apparent, and women’s perfume is what its color is apparent and hidden.” \His smell\"""""""
"9050","Muhammad bin Ali bin Maymun Al-Raqqi told us, he said: Muhammad bin Yusuf told us, meaning Al-Faryabi, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Al-Taffawi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “A man’s perfume is as long as his scent is apparent and his color is hidden. And perfume for women is as long as its color is apparent and its scent is subtle.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9051","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Waki’, he said: Azra bin Thabit told us, on the authority of Thumama bin Abdullah bin Anas, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when perfume was brought he would not return it.”"
"9052","Ubayd Allah bin Fadalah bin Ibrahim told me. He said: I am Abdullah bin Yazid al-Muqri. He said: Saeed is the son of Abi Ayyub. He said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Jaafar told me, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “Who “Some perfume is offered to him, but he does not reject it, for it is light in nature and has a pleasant smell.”"
"9053","Abdul Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam told us, he said: Shababah bin Siwar told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of 5 Khalid bin Jafar He is trustworthy 5, on the authority of Abu Nadrah, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, a woman from Bani “Israel took a gold ring and stuffed it with musk.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is the best of perfume.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9054","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Ghazwan told me, and he was Qarad, he said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Khalid. Ibn Ja'far, and Al-Mustamil Al-Basri, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa'id, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned a woman who had an intercourse with her He concluded it with musk, and said: “It is the best of perfume.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9055","Muhammad bin Omar bin Ali bin Muqaddam informed us, saying: Zakaria bin Yahya bin Yahya bin Amara Al-Ansari told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Suhaib, On the authority of Anas, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade a man from shaving saffron on his skin.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9056","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Anas, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade For a man to suffocate.”"
"9057","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Imran bin Dhabyan, on the authority of Hakim bin Saad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: A man came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he was wearing a shield from other creatures. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “Go, and he will wear him out.” Then he came to him. So he said: “Go, and wear him out.” Then he came to him, and he said: “Go, and wear him out.” Then he came to him, and said: “Go, and wear him out, and then do not come back.” \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"9058","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, he said: I heard Abu Hafs bin Amr, then he said: After him, he narrated, on the authority of Ali bin Murrah, that he passed by the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was in a state of confusion, and he said “Do you have a wife?” I said: No. He said: “So wash him, then wash him, then do not come back.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9059","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ata’, he said: I heard Abu Hafs Omar, on the authority of Ya’la bin Once, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a man in a disheveled state, and he said: “Go and wash him, then wash him, and do not come back.” Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Amr, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ali, Towards him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9060","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr ibn Musawar told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Hafs, on the authority of Ya’la ibn Al-Thaqafi once said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw me with a presence of a male or female being, and he said: “O Ali, do you have a woman?” I said: No. He said: “Wash it, then do not repeat it. Then wash it, then do not repeat it. Then wash it, then do not repeat it.” He said: So I washed it, then do not repeat it. I returned, then I washed it, then I did not repeat it, then I washed it, then I did not repeat it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9061","Ismail bin Yaqoub Al-Subhi told me, he said: Muhammad bin Musa bin Ayan told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Hafs, on the authority of Ya’la, said: I passed by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while I was wearing saffron, and he said: “Ya’la, can you A woman?” I said: No. He said: “Go and wash him, then wash him, then wash him, then do not come back.” He said: So I went and washed him. Then I washed it, then I washed it, then I did not wash it again. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9062","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Thabit, who is Ibn Amara, told us, on the authority of Ghunaim bin Qays, on the authority of Al-Ash’ari said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Any woman who perfumes herself and passes by some people so that they can smell her scent is an adulteress.” \"" 9063"""""
"9063","Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Ibrahim informed us, saying: Sulayman narrated to us—and he is ibn Dawud ibn 'Ali ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-'Abbas al-Hashimi—saying: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd informed us, saying: I heard Safwan ibn Sulaym—and I heard nothing from Safwan other than this—narrating, from five trustworthy men, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""When a woman goes out to the mosque, let her not wear perfume, just as she would bathe from major ritual impurity (janabah)."" Abridged."
"9064","Muhammad bin Hisham bin Issa Al-Baghdadi told us, he said: Abu Alqamah Al-Farwi Abdullah bin Muhammad told us, he said: Yazid bin Khusaifa, on the authority of Busr bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Any woman who burns incense, Do not attend the afterlife with us.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: We do not know that anyone followed Yazid bin Khusaifa on what he said: on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and Yaqoub bin Abd disagreed with him. Allah bin Al-Ashjaj narrated it, on the authority of Busr bin Saeed, on the authority of Zainab Al-Thaqfiya (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9065","Hilal bin Al-Ala bin Hilal told me, he said: Mu’alla bin Asad Al-Basri told us, he said: Wahib told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Yaqoub Bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Busr bin Saeed, on the authority of Zainab, Abdullah’s wife, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said For women: “If one of you attends the evening prayer, do not touch perfume.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9066","Ubayd Allah ibn Sa`id told us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa`id told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, he said: Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashjaj narrated to me, on the authority of Busr bin Saeed, on the authority of Zainab, Abdullah’s wife, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you attends the dinner Do not touch perfume.”"
"9067","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Jarir bin Abdul Hamid, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Bukayr bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Busr bin Saeed, on the authority of Zainab, Abdullah’s wife, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you attends the dinner Do not touch perfume.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: The hadith of Yahya bin Saeed and Jarir is more authentic than the hadith of Wahib bin Khalid, and God Almighty knows best."
"9068","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Ja’far, on the authority of Bukayr bin Abdullah Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Busr Bin Saeed, on the authority of Zainab Al-Thaqfiya, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever goes out to the mosque, do not offer perfume.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9069","Ahmad bin Saeed bin Yaqoub Al-Homsi told me, he said: Othman bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Bukayr bin Al-Ashjaj, On the authority of Busr bin Saeed, on the authority of Zainab Al-Thaqafiyya, that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you go out to the mosque, do not “You may offer yourselves in goodness.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: The hadith of Qutaibah is more authentic than the one after it, and God knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9070","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Saad told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Qurashi, on the authority of Bukair bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Busr bin Saeed, on the authority of Zainab Al-Thaqafiyyah, the wife of Abdullah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “commanded her” “That she should not touch perfume when she goes out for the afterlife.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9071","Ahmad bin Saeed Al-Rubati told us, he said: Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Ubayy told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Amr bin Hisham, on the authority of Bukayr bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Busr bin Saeed, said: Zainab Al-Thaqafiyya, a woman, told me Abdullah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to her: “When you go out for dinner, do not feel fresh.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9072","Abu Bakr bin Ali told us, he said: Mansour bin Abi Muzahim told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Saad told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Amr bin Hisham, on the authority of Bukayr, on the authority of Busr bin Saeed, on the authority of Zainab Al-Thaqfiya, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He said: “If a woman goes out for the afterlife, she should not touch perfume.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: The hadith of Ya’qub is more likely to be correct, and God knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9073","Yusuf bin Sa`id told me, he said: He informed me, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Ziyad bin Sa`d informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Busr Ibn Saeed, on the authority of Zainab Al-Thaqafiyya, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When one of you witnesses the prayer, do not touch perfume.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is not preserved from the hadith of al-Zuhri, and God knows best."
"9074","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh Abu Tahir informed us, saying: Ibn Wahb informed us, saying: Makhramah informed me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: Ibn Umar used to “if he cleaned his body with an unpeeled aloe, and with camphor, he would throw it with the aloe, then he said: Thus The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to perform ijtimar"
"9075","Wahb bin Bayan told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Amr bin Al-Harith told us, that Abu Ashanah is Al-Ma’afiri. He told him that he heard Uqba bin Amir tell that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was withholding jewelry and silk from his family. He says: “If you love the jewelery and silk of Paradise, do not wear them in this world.”"
